README for 2026-08-04 primary elections.

I. Finding, getting, and storing the data from the county election reports.

   All of this is done in the ElectionImport project, currently checked-out from
   git and set up on the mivoter.org server, user elections, in the ElectionImport directory.

   The "top of ticket" races (Governor, US Senate, state house, state senate, etc.) 
   are automatically downloaded from other sources, and require little manual handling.
   So this section is all about the county (and below) level races.

   1. Tracking the data.
      The tracking spreadsheet for the primary election county data is at:
      https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1tQl_3ekd6uBhWYle5eNGthreMqoJj8LS7ARjkUaDkkM/edit?gid=158379855#gid=158379855

      Green bars are 1st priority counties; yellow bars are 2nd priority.  Everything else is 3rd priority.

   2. Recording county clerk election pages.
      This time around, we're saving the page that, in turn, points to the actual primary election results URL.
      This way, come November, we can (presumably) start from THAT page, to find the general election results
      URL.

   3. Actual election results.
      We have several 'flavors' of election results URLs, which are in turn indicated by the "page type"
      column:
         Vendor Page (w/ Result)  -- the vendor page (notably EnhancedVoting) that in turn contains
                                     results for multiple elections.  Our download scripts start from
                                     there to get the final, machine-readable, result (usually JSON).

         Vendor Page (NO Results) -- same as above, except there are NO results for this election there (yet).
       
         ACTUAL Results           -- the URL of the actual results, typically a PDF file.

   4. Getting and saving the data.
      The actual method of downloading the data depends on the data format.  The results must
      be stored in the PRIMARIES subdirectory, under a sub-sub-directory with the county name.
      The filename format fits the standard that we've used for previous elections, e.g.
      11-berrien_2026-08-04.json.ph1.json or 70-ottawa_2026-08-04.clarity.ph1.csv.

      a. Enhanced voting:
            fetchEnhancedPrimaryResults  countyid  countyname
         where countyid is the county # from the master spreadsheet, and countyname is EXACTLY
         the name as shown in the enhancedvoting.com URL (e.g. just "berrien", not "berrien-county-mi")

         The script automatically stores the file in the proper PRIMARIES directory.

      b. Clarity:
         These downloads are currently all done manually.  On the page for the election report,
         on the right, there is a link for "Summary CSV" download.  The download is typically
         a "summary.zip" file; unzip it, then place and rename the resulting CSV file in the
         proper PRIMARIES subdirectory, e.g. eaton/23-eaton_2026-08-04.clarity.ph1.csv.

      c. PDF:
         These downloads are currently all done manually (although they could be scripted).
         The URL in the "August 2026 election report URL" should be the PDF, or automatically
         get redirected to the PDF.  Click on it, then download or "save as" a PDF file.
         Place it in the proper PRIMARIES subdirectory, e.g. bay/03-bay_2026-08-04.pdf.ph1.pdf.
 
